##! Please refer to the documentation at
##! https://coreruleset.org/docs/development/regex_assembly/.

##! The command must fill its own line: it follows the line break, optionally after
##! a short tag (`A1 QUIT`), and nothing but spaces may follow it before the next
##! line break or the end of the value. Matching the word anywhere on the line made
##! ordinary multi-line text such as "...\r\nCan you help with the data?" match.
##!+ i
##!^ \r\n(?:\w{1,20} )?
##!$ [ \t]*(?:[\r\n]|$)

##! - SMTP Commands without or optional params
DATA
QUIT
HELP(?: \S{1,64})?

##! - SMTP Commands with params

##! Not covered -  X<atom> Command (client extensions)
